.Dd October 23, 2026
.Dt LN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ln
.Nd create links
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl fs
.Op Fl L Ns | Ns Fl P
.Ar target
.Op Ar linkname
.Pp
.Nm
.Op Fl fs
.Op Fl L Ns | Ns Fl P
.Ar target ...
.Ar directory
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
creates a link for
.Ar target
at
.Ar linkname .
.Pp
if multiple targets are specified, the last operand must be an existing
.Ar directory
and a link to each
.Ar target
is created inside of it, using the target's basename.
.Pp
if no
.Ar linkname
is specified, link
.Ar target
under its basename in the current directory.
.Pp
the options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f
force the creation of the link by removing any files by the same name.
.It Fl s
create a symlink
.It Fl L
when creating a hard link for a symbolic link,
create a hard link for the target of the symbolic link.
.It Fl P
when creating a hard link for a symbolic link,
create a hard link for the symbolic link itself.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh AUTHORS
.An juanvel400
